&lt;p&gt;As&amp;nbsp;Employment Counsel (EMEA), you will serve as Figma&#39;s primary employment legal advisor across EMEA, partnering closely with People and business leaders to support our international workforce and help scale our global employment legal function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from our London Hub or remotely in the United Kingdom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary employment legal advisor for EMEA and support other regional and global employment matters, partnering closely with People and business leaders on strategic employment and workforce matters&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, revise, and update employment and benefits-related documentation and agreements as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise senior stakeholders on complex employee relations, disciplinary, grievance and investigation matters and recommend appropriate outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and operationalise compliance-based requirements and build scalable employment-related policies, playbooks, templates, and self-serve tools in collaboration with partner teams to help scale the legal function and the business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Figma&#39;s international growth, including expansion into new jurisdictions, workforce scaling initiatives, and evolving employment compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage employment-related litigation including strategy, discovery, drafting, and coordination with external counsel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and address developing employment legal requirements and potential future legal risks to the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other cross-functional business teams including legal, accounting, procurement, and communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to hear from you if you have/are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UK-qualified with 8+ years PQE, including experience at a top-tier law firm and in-house legal department practising employment law&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience providing practical, commercially focused employment law advice across EMEA, including employee relations, investigations, works councils and consultation requirements, restructurings, redundancies, dismissals, and other complex employment matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build trusted relationships with People, Legal, and business leaders, exercise strong commercial judgement, and influence decision-making in complex situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and scaling employment policies, programmes, processes, and documentation in a growing organisation, including leveraging technology and AI-enabled tools where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, intellectual curiosity, and a collaborative approach, with a strong desire to learn, improve, and help build effective solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
