&lt;p&gt;Success in this role requires deep Workday expertise, experience managing delivery across internal teams and external implementation partners, and the ability to establish effective processes for project intake, prioritization, sprint planning, and resource management. We&#39;re looking for a leader who understands how Workday connects to the broader People Technology ecosystem and is excited to evolve our systems, processes, and team as our organization grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do at Figma:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of HRIS Specialists by building technical depth through cross-training, documentation, and shared ownership across Workday functional areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the team&#39;s operating model, including project intake, prioritization, sprint planning, capacity planning, and release management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage work across internal HRIS team members and external implementation partners, balancing quality, speed, and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide governance and technical oversight for Workday configuration, while contributing hands-on configuration for complex, high-impact, or business-critical initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with People, Payroll, IT, Finance, and other cross-functional teams to understand business needs and deliver integrated solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve processes, automate manual work, and increase operational efficiency across the systems ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging technologies and features, including AI-enabled capabilities, and recommend solutions that enhance the employee and people team experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the evolution of our broader technology ecosystem by ensuring Workday integrates effectively with the systems that support our Figmates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
