&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you&#39;re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you&#39;re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Product Designer to join our Design Systems (Figma Pattern Library) team, dedicated to building and evolving shared patterns and components across Figma’s expanding suite of products. This role will focus on a consistent and approachable experience for Figma’s audience, regardless of the product they are using. As Figma continues to grow, a cohesive design system that spans multiple products is critical. We are looking for a designer with experience in multi-product environments who can work collaboratively across teams to develop, refine, and implement design systems that scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the overall strategy and decision-making regarding cross-product design systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and communicate a clear vision for shared design patterns that can be utilized across various products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product management, engineering, and other design teams to ensure consistent implementation of design components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, iterate, and refine design system components, including flows, prototypes, and high-fidelity visuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the adoption and continuous improvement of the design system across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
